Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.95,0:05:54.45,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(675,0)\fnTimes New Roman\bord1.5\shad0\c&HFFFFFF&\fs24\an1\3c&H262C29&\pos(48,310)}Class C Entrants:\NYukimura, Hirata, Wang, Kushida
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.45,0:05:59.96,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(675,0)\fnTimes New Roman\bord1.5\shad0\c&HFFFFFF&\fs24\pos(320,20)\an8\3c&H3C423E&}Round 5: Archery
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.96,0:06:03.46,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(675,0)\fnTimes New Roman\bord1.5\shad0\c&HFFFFFF&\fs24\an1\3c&H262C29&\pos(56,331.692)}Class C Entrant:\NMiyake
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.87,0:06:05.46,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Quite impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:06.61,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Just one more!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,5)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs16\bord0\shad0}Final Special Exam
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs24\bord0\shad0\pos(225,64)\c&HF6F7F6&}3x3 Basketball
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnTimes New Roman\b0\fs22\bord0\shad0\c&HF6F7F6&\b1\pos(318,120)}Typing
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnTimes New Roman\b0\fs22\bord0\shad0\c&HF6F7F6&\b1\pos(318,160)}English
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnTimes New Roman\b0\fs22\bord0\shad0\c&HF6F7F6&\b1\pos(318,198)}Math
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.46,0:06:07.71,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnTimes New Roman\b0\fs22\bord0\shad0\c&HF6F7F6&\b1\pos(318,235)}Archery
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.61,0:06:08.30,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Yes! We're almost there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.30,0:06:11.72,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,We're winning all the subjects we submitted!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.72,0:06:13.39,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.39,0:06:15.98,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,If we get a good pull on the next subject...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.98,0:06:18.46,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,The next competition will be...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.44,0:06:19.60,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,90)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord0\shad0}Round 6
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.44,0:06:19.60,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\shad0\1a&HFF&\fnTimes New Roman\3c&HFFFFFF&\pos(320,160)\b1}Mental Math
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.60,0:06:21.33,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,It's one of theirs?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.71,0:06:21.99,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Oh, no...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.35,0:06:23.86,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,Choose the students to participate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.28,0:06:27.69,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I suppose I can't afford to lose this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.53,0:06:32.55,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Our participants will be Tamiya Emi-san
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.39,0:06:36.12,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(225,0)\pos(180,190)\an8\c&H75655E&\3c&HFAF8EC&\fnTimes New Roman\shad0\fs22\bord1\b1}Tamiya Emi
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.55,0:06:36.12,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,and Katsuragi Kohei-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.42,0:06:37.37,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.71,0:06:40.03,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'll go with Matsushita Chiaki
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.37,0:06:43.09,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\fnTimes New Roman\shad0\fs22\bord1.5\b1\move(271,210,185,210)}Matsushita Chiaki
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.37,0:06:43.09,Main,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\fnTimes New Roman\shad0\fs22\bord1.5\b1\move(576,210,494,210)\alpha&HFF&\t(1073,1406,1 \alpha&H00&)}Koenji Rokusuke
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.70,0:06:42.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and Koenji Rokusuke.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.09,0:06:46.10,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I see. Because the rule is that the \Nwinner isn't decided by combined score,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.09,0:06:50.09,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(675,0)\fnTimes New Roman\bord1.5\shad0\c&HFFFFFF&\fs24\pos(320,20)\an8\3c&H3C423E&}Round 6: Mental Math
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.10,0:06:50.09,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,but by the single student \Nwith the highest score.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.71,0:06:53.37,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,The plan is that even if Koenji-kun \Ndoesn't take it seriously,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.37,0:06:56.31,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Matsushita-san is there to cover him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.67,0:06:58.85,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,There will be ten questions in all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.85,0:07:03.14,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,The further you go, the harder they will \Nbecome, but the more they will be worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.96,0:07:05.11,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,Begin!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.61,0:07:09.61,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord0\shad0\fs16\an5\pos(374,318)\fay.03\frx0\fry332}Final Special Exam Round 6\N{\fs28}Question 1
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.87,0:07:13.40,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Huh? What the...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.11,0:07:14.54,Main,Hashimoto,0,0,0,,Hang on, that's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.73,0:07:15.06,Main,Onodera,0,0,0,,All of those?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.54,0:07:16.37,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,There's not enough time!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.06,0:07:16.37,Main,Hondo,0,0,0,,I couldn't remember them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.88,0:07:26.50,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,That damn Koenji...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.50,0:07:27.88,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,He's not taking it seriously at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.12,0:07:29.49,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Koenji-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.13,0:07:34.64,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(497,108)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\bord0\shad0\frx354\fry358\frz359}End
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.13,0:07:34.64,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\bord0\shad0\pos(152,108)\frx348\fry0\frz0.4834}End
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.74,0:07:32.44,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,That was all ten questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.44,0:07:34.18,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,Pencils down.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.92,0:07:38.28,Main,Hoshinomiya,0,0,0,,Did they not even try to \Nsolve those last ones?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.52,0:07:44.65,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,The captains' rule is that the captain \Nmay answer one question themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.65,0:07:47.81,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I'll answer question 10.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.21,0:07:46.96,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,150)\fs14\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\pos(300.666,64.667)}Select question to answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.00,0:07:49.64,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(75,0)\fs14\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\pos(300.666,64.667)}Please enter your answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.81,0:07:49.64,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,What about you, Ayanokoji-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.64,0:07:50.51,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,150)\fs20\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\pos(442,102)}Select question to answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.96,0:07:51.47,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'll do the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.55,0:07:51.90,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,0)\fs20\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\pos(440,102)}Please enter your answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.41,0:07:58.63,Italics,Koenji,0,0,0,,I've never tried it before, but it's \Nquite an amusing little pastime.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.56,0:08:01.91,Italics,Koenji,0,0,0,,The answer to the last question
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.91,0:08:05.42,Italics,Koenji,0,0,0,,is 7,619, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.42,0:08:07.36,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.42,0:08:09.17,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fs24\b1\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\pos(320,80)}Please enter your answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.36,0:08:09.17,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Isn't that a surprise?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.67,0:08:13.18,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,I will now announce the results.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.18,0:08:16.70,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,The top placer is Katsuragi Kohei.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.18,0:08:19.68,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs6\shad0\b1\3c&H141111&\pos(345.334,109.333)}1st: Katsuragi Kohei\N 2nd: Matsushita Chiaki\N 3rd: Tamiya Emi\N 4th: Koenji Rokusuke
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.70,0:08:18.73,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,The winner is Class A.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.73,0:08:20.73,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Guess it's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.68,0:08:20.84,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.93,0:08:21.18,Main_Top,Wang,0,0,0,,Koenji-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.46,0:08:25.19,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I told Katsuragi-kun in advance...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.19,0:08:31.18,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,that if he betrayed us, I'd have a \Nhard-working Class A student expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.20,0:08:36.20,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs16\3c&H191914&\shad0\pos(365.333,26.667)}Final Special Exam Round 6\N Mental Math
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.20,0:08:36.20,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HF2E7D5&\3c&H574029&\shad0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs16\an6\pos(134,225.334)}Matsushita Chiaki\NKoenji Rokusuke\N Katsuragi Kohei\N Tamiya Emi
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.51,0:08:44.21,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I'm glad Koenji-kun didn't take it seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.21,0:08:46.28,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,When you don't have control \Nover a kind of power,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.28,0:08:48.52,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you can't integrate it into your strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.52,0:08:49.75,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.63,0:08:53.47,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Still, it's three against three now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.87,0:08:57.72,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You caught up to us, \Nbut you don't seem happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.72,0:09:03.06,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Because after this last subject, \Nour fun time together will end.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.48,0:09:07.80,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,That just leaves...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.23,0:09:12.26,Main,Sakagami,0,0,0,,I will now announce the \Nseventh and final subject.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.99,0:09:14.74,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,40)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord0\shad0}Round 7
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.99,0:09:14.74,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\shad0\fnTimes New Roman\3c&HFFFFFF&\pos(320,140)\b1\c&H000000&}Chess
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.29,0:09:18.49,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,To think this would be the \Nfinal subject chosen...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.49,0:09:26.75,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnTimes New Roman\b1\shad0\3c&H583C29&\pos(381.334,6.667)\frx352\fry8}Captains' Special Rule
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.49,0:09:26.75,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\shad0\3c&H583C29&\an8\fay-.027\pos(368.667,98)\frx2\fry8}The captain can freely give instructions to the \Nplayer for up to 30 minutes of the allotted time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.71,0:09:22.24,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,A rule that gives the captains a \Nlot of time to give instructions...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.24,0:09:26.75,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Which means the battle will \Nbe between the two of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.75,0:09:30.50,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to tell you, chess is my specialty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.78,0:09:32.58,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.01,0:09:34.57,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,What a happy coincidence.
